    {
      "name": "4 — Phase 3: Interview Lifecycle & Candidate Join",
      "description": "Drives one interview through its full lifecycle (schedule -> regenerate link -> join-token validation -> lobby before admit -> admit -> lobby after admit -> reschedule -> cross-org 404 -> revoke link -> cancel) using recruiter A (org A) and the public, no-auth join-token endpoints, then covers the reachable join-token refusal branches (NOT_FOUND, REVOKED, OUTSIDE_WINDOW).\n\nPrerequisite: run folder '2 — Auth (Keycloak)' first so {{accessToken}} holds recruiter A's token. Set recruiterAPassword in Collection -> Variables before running.\n\nState is captured in collection variables and used by later requests in this folder:\n- {{interviewId}} — the live interview (org A)\n- {{rawToken}} — its current join token (revoked on reschedule/revoke/cancel)\n- {{bogusToken}} — arbitrary token that never exists (NOT_FOUND)\n- {{pastInterviewId}} / {{pastRawToken}} — a separate interview scheduled in the past, whose token falls outside its validity window (OUTSIDE_WINDOW)\n\nEvery schedule/reschedule/cancel/regenerate here also publishes a Kafka event, so check MailHog (http://localhost:8025) for the corresponding candidate emails (Step B proof).\n\nUSED and EXPIRED are refusal branches in PublicJoinService.resolveToken but are NOT reachable via any public HTTP endpoint in this phase (no endpoint marks a token USED, and nothing sets token status EXPIRED) — they are covered by unit tests only.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /api/interviews — schedule (recruiter A)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Schedule the interview near-term (now + 5 min) so its join token",
                  "// falls inside the validity window [start-15m, start+30m] while the",
                  "// public validate/lobby requests run. A far-future start makes the",
                  "// token OUTSIDE_WINDOW until 15 minutes before the interview.",
                  "var start = new Date(Date.now() + 5 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('scheduledStart', start);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 201', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "var json = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('body.id is a UUID', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.id).to.match(/^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('body.status equals SCHEDULED', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.status).to.eql('SCHEDULED');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('body.admitted equals false', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(json.admitted).to.eql(false);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('interviewId', json.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"firstName\": \"Jane\",\n    \"lastName\": \"Candidate\",\n    \"email\": \"jane@example.com\",\n    \"phone\": \"\"\n  },\n  \"scheduledStart\": \"{{scheduledStart}}\",\n  \"durationMinutes\": 60,\n  \"segments\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Intro\",\n      \"orderIndex\": 0,\n      \"plannedMinutes\": 15,\n      \"preparedQuestions\": [\"Tell me about yourself\"]\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{gatewayUrl}}/api/interviews",
              "host": [
                "{{gatewayUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "interviews"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Recruiter A schedules an interview starting ~5 minutes from now (so its join token stays inside its validity window for the public tests below). Captures {{interviewId}}. Publishes interview.scheduled (check MailHog)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
